// Title: Service Control Manager Started a Shell or Script Host
// ATT&CK: T1569.002 | Tactic: Execution | Sigma id: e55e1c9b-bcf9-479e-bc4d-9bdb660bbab4
// Data source: DeviceProcessEvents (Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / Defender XDR connector)
// Severity: High
// False positives: Services of backup and management products whose binary path is a script (review and allowlist)
// Suggested analytics rule: run every 15m, look back 30m, alert when results > 0.
// Entity mapping: Host = DeviceName, Account = AccountName, Process = ProcessCommandLine
// The time filter below is for ad-hoc hunting; the analytics rule's lookback applies when scheduled.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\services.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe")
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine
